[size=6][b]✩ Dynamic Camera[/b][/size]

[url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UHV4UTi0Kd4][img]https://img.youtube.com/vi/UHV4UTi0Kd4/maxresdefault.jpg[/img][/url]

Subtle dynamic camera and first-person viewmodel (hands) inertia for OpenMW. More natural movement and jumping.

Target lock with shader effects (bokeh) and a sneak shader (vignette). Immersive cell transition effects (bokeh). Experimental strafe camera tilt effects (disabled by default). Highly customizable.

Meant to be used with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56584]Dynamic Reticle[/url] mod, but will work without it.

[i]1st-person animations in the video are from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation v2[/url] and MCAR. Circular reticle, HP widget, sneak reticle and hit markers are from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56584]Dynamic Reticle[/url].[/i]

[size=5][b]✩ Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Slight headbob when jumping and landing.
[*]Viewmodel inertia when looking around.
[*]Visual and sound effects when moving at high speeds (mainly to enhance the feel of big, long leaps).
[*]Target lock (set the key bind in the script settings) with a neat DOF bokeh shader active only during the lock. Lock distance and switching targets by moving the mouse/stick are adjustable.
[*]Immersive bokeh/darkening animated transition when entering or leaving interiors.
[*]Sneak vignette.
[*]A few [b]extra effects[/b] - cinematic black bars on target lock and camera roll on strafing. They are disabled by default and can be turned on in the settings.
[*][b]Full Body Awareness tweaks[/b] - if you play with a visible body in first person using the FBA Compatibility folder of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation[/url], these tweaks are applied automatically to make the experience more coherent and prevent some visual clipping.
[*]All of it is adjustable in Options -> Scripts -> Dynamic Caméra.
[/list]

[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/DynamicCameraOpenmw/main/imgs/morrowind_kofi_banner_left_half_bright124.gif[/img][/url][url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/DynamicCameraOpenmw/main/imgs/nexus/banner_right.png[/img][/url]
[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/DynamicCameraOpenmw/main/imgs/nexus/banner_glow.png[/img][/url]

[size=5][b]✩ How to install[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Requires OpenMW 0.49 or newer.[/b]
[*]Install and enable [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60256]Max Yari's Script Services (MSS)[/url], it's a required dependency.
[*]Install this mod [b]with a mod organiser[/b]: download the archive (or this repository as an archive) and drag and drop it into your mod organiser of choice (e.g [url=https://github.com/ModOrganizer2/modorganizer/releases]Mod Organizer 2[/url] on Windows or [url=https://github.com/grazelandsnomad/nerevarine_organizer/releases/tag/v0.70]Nerevarine Organizer[/url] on Linux). [b]Or[/b] [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]read this tutorial[/url] on how to install mods using the launcher or completely manually (it's also very easy).
[*]Enable [font=Courier New]DynamicCamera.omwscripts[/font] in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher.
[*]Ensure that post processing is enabled: Options -> Video -> Post Processing (in-game) or "Enable post processing" in the "Visuals" tab of the launcher settings. The shader effects don't show without it.
[*]Set a key bind for target lock in Options -> Scripts -> Dynamic Caméra.
[/list]

Have fun!

[size=5][b]✩ ReAnimation and Full Body Awareness[/b][/size]

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/56625]Full Body Awareness[/url] are supported. With ReAnimation's FBA Compatibility folder installed, so that your own body is visible in first person, this mod adapts the camera to it: the hands stop short of sinking into your chest when you look down, and the camera eases forward so you see past your chest instead of into your armor's neck opening.

Nothing needs to be set up - the FBA Compatibility folder is detected automatically, and the settings page tells you whether it was found.

[size=5][b]✩ Known issues[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]With OpenMW's 360° third-person camera, if a target is locked while your weapon is not drawn, moving around switches between targets. It only happens with the weapon sheathed and the 360° camera. Can be "fixed" by disabling look-based target switching in setting.
[/list]

